# ReClaim AI - Client environment
# Copy to `.env` and fill in.
#
# WARNING: every VITE_* value here is inlined into the production JavaScript
# bundle and is readable by anyone who loads the site. Only put values here
# that are safe to publish. No LLM keys, no service accounts, no secrets.

# ---------- API ----------
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:3001

# ---------- Firebase web config ----------
# These are public by design; access is controlled by Firebase security rules
# and by an authorized-domain allowlist, not by hiding these values.
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_MEASUREMENT_ID=

# ---------- Maps ----------
# Geoapify browser key. Restrict it by HTTP referrer in the Geoapify console.
VITE_GEOAPIFY_API_KEY=

# ---------- Deprecated, but still required today ----------
# These are live reads in the current code, so leaving them blank produces a
# working build with silently degraded behaviour:
#   - the two LLM keys make aiService fall through to its no-key branch, so
#     image analysis and description enhancement stop working in the report and
#     add-item modals (client/src/services/aiService.ts)
#   - VITE_ADMIN_EMAIL is the filter that hides the admin account from the admin
#     Users list; blank means the admin sees itself in the list
#     (client/src/services/userService.ts)
#
# Set them to run the app as it stands today. Track A phase 5 deletes all three:
# it moves LLM calls to server endpoints (defect SEC-16, keys are readable by
# anyone who loads the site) and replaces the email filter with a role check
# (defect SEC-21). Do not build anything new on top of them.
VITE_GROQ_API_KEY=
VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY=
VITE_ADMIN_EMAIL=
